              "help": {
                "text": "Validating certificate chains which use policies is unexpectedly inefficient when certificates in the chain contain a very large number of policy mappings, possibly causing denial of service.\n\nThis only affects validation of otherwise trusted certificate chains, issued by a root CA in the VerifyOptions.Roots CertPool, or in the system certificate pool.\n",
                "markdown": "> Validating certificate chains which use policies is unexpectedly inefficient when certificates in the chain contain a very large number of policy mappings, possibly causing denial of service.\n\nThis only affects validation of otherwise trusted certificate chains, issued by a root CA in the VerifyOptions.Roots CertPool, or in the system certificate pool.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.24.6  |\n|Affected range  <1.25.9                   |\n|Fixed version   1.25.9                    |\n"
