            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-78663",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-78663"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-78663?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.26.9",
              "help": {
                "text": "The HTTP/2 server can refund connection-level flow control twice for the same data: Once when a client resets a stream (refunding data for any sent-but-unread portion of the stream), and again when a request handler reads the buffered data. A malicious client can exploit this to bypass the configured connection-level flow control limit (MaxReceiveBufferPerConnection). Total buffered data is still limited by the concurrent stream limit and stream-level flow control.\n",
                "markdown": "> The HTTP/2 server can refund connection-level flow control twice for the same data: Once when a client resets a stream (refunding data for any sent-but-unread portion of the stream), and again when a request handler reads the buffered data. A malicious client can exploit this to bypass the configured connection-level flow control limit (MaxReceiveBufferPerConnection). Total buffered data is still limited by the concurrent stream limit and stream-level flow control.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.24.6  |\n|Affected range  <1.26.9                   |\n|Fixed version   1.26.9                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.26.9",
                "cvssV3_severity": "CRITICAL",
                "fixed_version": "1.26.9",
                "purls": [
