            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39821",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-39821"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-39821?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.25.13",
              "help": {
                "text": "The ToASCII and ToUnicode functions incorrectly accept Punycode-encoded labels that decode to an ASCII-only label. For example, ToUnicode(\"xn--example-.com\") incorrectly returns the name \"example.com\" rather than an error.\n\nThis behavior can lead to privilege escalation in programs using the idna package. For example, a program which performs privilege checks on the ASCII hostname may reject \"example.com\" but permit \"xn--example-.com\". If that program subsequently converts the ASCII hostname to Unicode, it will inadvertently permits access to the Unicode name \"example.com\".\n",
                "markdown": "> The ToASCII and ToUnicode functions incorrectly accept Punycode-encoded labels that decode to an ASCII-only label. For example, ToUnicode(\"xn--example-.com\") incorrectly returns the name \"example.com\" rather than an error.\n\nThis behavior can lead to privilege escalation in programs using the idna package. For example, a program which performs privilege checks on the ASCII hostname may reject \"example.com\" but permit \"xn--example-.com\". If that program subsequently converts the ASCII hostname to Unicode, it will inadvertently permits access to the Unicode name \"example.com\".\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.24.6  |\n|Affected range  <1.25.13                  |\n|Fixed version   1.25.13                   |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.25.13",
                "cvssV3_severity": "CRITICAL",
                "fixed_version": "1.25.13",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.24.6"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.6",
                "tags": [
                  "CRITICAL"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56857",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-56857"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-56857?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.26.9",
              "help": {
                "text": "On Windows, when the target of Root.Mkdir or Root.MkdirAll is a junction pointing to an empty location, the operation can create a directory at the junction target even when that target is located outside the root. This only applies to operations where the last path component is a junction (path/to/junction, but not path/junction/target).\n",
                "markdown": "> On Windows, when the target of Root.Mkdir or Root.MkdirAll is a junction pointing to an empty location, the operation can create a directory at the junction target even when that target is located outside the root. This only applies to operations where the last path component is a junction (path/to/junction, but not path/junction/target).\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.24.6  |\n|Affected range  <1.26.9                   |\n|Fixed version   1.26.9                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.26.9",
                "cvssV3_severity": "CRITICAL",
                "fixed_version": "1.26.9",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.24.6"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8",
                "tags": [
